    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d873">

                <pb facs="0756" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48/3201a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-01-24T18:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>176. In your discretion please discuss with the appropriate German authorities
                    the difficulties now being encountered by the American Red Cross in the matter
                    of relief in Poland. For details see Department’s 167, January 23, 11
                        p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d873-f1"/> You may point out that the requests of
                    the American Red Cross in nowise involve any lack of confidence in the German
                    Red Cross, but represent a normal procedure where responsibility is assumed
                    toward executive committee, donors, et cetera. Norman Davis<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d873-f2"/> has had a long talk with Thomsen<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d873-f3"/> who volunteered to send a telegram to his Government
                    urging it to accept the American Red Cross viewpoint; Thomsen suggested that at
                    the same time we authorize you to make an official approach.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d873-f1" n="1" xml:id="d873-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. The American Red Cross sought assurances that its delegate would be
                    permitted to cooperate with the German Red Cross in receiving and allocating
                    supplies for impartial distribution through Polish agencies. It requested that
                    it be given adequate receipts for the supplies that had already been delivered.
                    (840.48/3199)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d873-f2" n="2" xml:id="d873-f2-content">
                <p>Chairman of the American Red Cross.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d873-f3" n="3" xml:id="d873-f3-content">
                <p>Hans Thomsen, German Chargé.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
